# Tick-mode lockstep regression
#
# Variant of emulator_smoke that opts into deterministic-time lockstep:
# the bridge advances simavr only when klippy's reactor sends an
# `advance T` over its tick socket, and klippy doesn't process timers
# or fds past T until simavr has advanced there. This eliminates the
# host-load timing skew that makes the parallel sim_time path flaky on
# CPU-contended hosts. We reuse emulator_smoke.cfg unchanged - the
# only difference is the fixture's `tick_mode: true` flag.
#
# KNOWN BLOCKED under --force-emulator (clean-host finding). Two layers,
# one fixed and one still open:
#   1. FIXED: tick advance livelocked because the bridge truncated
#      target*freq to an integer cycle, stopping the AVR a fraction of a
#      cycle below a reactor.pause() wakeup time, so the greenlet never
#      fired and klippy re-requested the identical advance forever. The
#      bridge now advances to the first cycle strictly past the target
#      (simavr_bridge.c), and simulated time progresses correctly.
#   2. IMPLEMENTED but STILL FAILING: simavr_bridge.c now uses a
#      single-threaded synchronous host-link UART in tick mode (suart_*)
#      instead of uart_pty's real-time pump thread, so byte movement is
#      deterministic and free of the pump-vs-avr_run race. Verified that
#      klippy's serialqueue does receive the firmware's identify
#      responses through it (reads of 5/53/54 bytes). It still does not
#      complete identify: after ~2s of simulated time klippy's read
#      returns EOF while the bridge is mid-advance, and identify never
#      reaches "Loaded MCU". Root cause of that EOF (the master appears
#      open yet the slave read returns 0) is not yet isolated - the
#      Renode tick path, which is structurally identical, works
#      (stm32f103_tick). REQUIRES_EMULATOR, kept out of the default CMD;
#      it was only ever skipped before, so it never actually ran.
CONFIG emulator_smoke.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
EMULATOR emulator_tick_mode.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # assertions depend on real MCU responses;
# skipped (not degraded to fileoutput) when the emulator backend isn't built

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do periodic
# sht3x reads against the scripted fixture.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
